WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  marvel studios moon night has some  otherworldly action which is why i'm  breaking it down with vfx supervisor  sean faden hey sean hey lorraine now  let's kick off with episode two where we  see mr knight facing off against that  invisible jackal how did you and your  team first start to approach that scene  there was a lot of weight on this scene  and making sure that it um it landed  well it actually starts in the alleyways  you've got mr knight being sort of blown  through this fence we spent a lot of  time pre-visiting this scene because it  was he had the complications of having  to have an invisible opponent the jackal  is only visible you know occasionally  during this sequence we had a lot of  storyboards that we got from  one of our main storyboard artists phil  langone it wasn't for every single  sequence but when we did get them they  were extremely helpful in the end how we  shot it was we had a stunt person in a  gray suit pushing and pulling our stunt  moon knight or oscar and layla around  for me the the most important thing to  capture for real was leaping or landing  or running we did shoot when possible  references i think that if you end up  doing too much cg throughout every  single shot you end up losing some of  the reality so we always try to shoot  with real stunts  well we're talking battles we have to  talk about the end of the series where  we see your techniques taken to new  heights quite literally with a huge god  versus god battle in cairo how did you  go about approaching that scene and  bringing it to life it was a combination  of a lot of previs some storyboarding a  lot of back and forth with our stunt  team trying to figure out what the best  flow of fight choreography was going to  be for these moments and making sure  that we were seeing you know conscious  getting to be heroic and seeing amit use  some of her crocodile related fight  moves  we actually did a lot of work um within  the chamber of the gods because we have  a scene that takes place there where  controvers are normal size which means  they're actually you know nine feet tall  we had previous all this stuff and then  we went and we shot a lot of background  plates within our set which sometimes  are just looking at like a column and  the rest will be blue screen they  created costumes for ahmet and kanchi  real costumes that moved like the real  thing that looked like the real thing  that could be lit like the real thing so  it wasn't just guys in gray suits  running around we actually had a  lightable  concho and amit in our scene and they  were able to act against each other the  scale of the two characters mainly  became an issue when we were dealing  with other actors you need to interact  with them so if oscar was talking to  kanchu then kareem who played kancho on  set would be wearing an eyeline pole to  make him look nine feet tall it was  literally two ping-pong balls on the end  of a composite rod that was attached to  his uh like a lightweight vest that our  props department made  the gods are already quite tall but then  they grow even larger how did you create  this scene at such an epic scale so  they're almost as tall as the pyramids  and they're bashing around and wreaking  havoc  created a full cg giza plateau based on  some lidar that we had gotten from  disney archives we had a lot of work  that went into sort of figuring out just  how much dust or how much light should  be hitting these characters to make them  feel big and we found was like the less  light we put on them the more that we  should have played the light falling off  on them the bigger they they felt  this is really just a tiny drop in the  bucket of all of the action in the  series looking back are there any  moments that you think fans might have  missed the series is jam-packed with  lots of cool details i don't think  you're going to catch it on the first  viewing i really think it's one of those  things you have to watch a few times to  really appreciate all the detail and  heart that went into these moments all  right well i guess i'm going to have to  go start my re-watch right now so sean  thank you so much for talking with us  well i appreciate it thanks lorraine and  everyone be sure to go watch marvel  studios moon night all episodes are now  streaming only on disney plus  [Music]

